# Java Testing

## Stack

- JUnit 5 + Mockito: `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)`
- AssertJ for assertions — no raw `assertEquals`

## Test naming

```
methodName_scenario_expectedOutcome
```

Examples: `requireById_whenMissing_throwsNotFound`, `findAll_delegatesToRepository`

## Service tests

```java
@Mock private PlatformRepository platformRepository;
@InjectMocks private PlatformServiceImpl platformService;
```

- Mock the repository; verify delegation with `verify(repository).method()`
- Always test `requireById` for both found and missing cases

## Controller tests

- Use `@WebMvcTest(PlatformController.class)` for HTTP layer tests

## Assertions

```java
// ✅ GOOD
assertThat(result).containsExactly(entity);
assertThatThrownBy(() -> service.requireById("missing"))
    .isInstanceOf(ResponseStatusException.class);

// ❌ BAD
assertEquals(expected, actual);
```
